# Intentionally does NOT ignore dist/.
#
# compiler/.gitignore lists `dist/`, so the built output is never tracked. But
# npm-packlist honors a nested .gitignore even when the root package `files`
# whitelist lists `compiler/dist`, which would silently drop compiler/dist from
# the published tarball. A present .npmignore overrides the sibling .gitignore
# for npm only, so `compiler/dist` is packed while git keeps ignoring it. This
# file is load-bearing regardless of tracking: removing it drops compiler/dist
# from `npm pack` entirely.
